     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></span></p>\r\n<span></span>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>]\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Sarah Friedman<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Tuesday, December 19, 2017 1:34 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> geomorph R package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] Phylogenetically-corrected shape data<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">Hi all,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">For my current work, I&#39;m attempting to implement a similar method to the phylogenetically-transformed measure of morphological disparity used a recent paper by Serb et al. (2017). Following\r\n the Adams (2014) method, I believe I have correctly phylogenetically-transformed my shape data, but I&#39;m hoping someone would be willing to confirm this for me. Is my understanding correct in that multiplication of the shape data by the phylogenetic transformation\r\n matrix (E) results in &quot;phylogenetically-corrected&quot; shape data to which one could apply standard metrics of disparity? (code below if needed). I don&#39;t want to do a regression, which is why I haven&#39;t used the geomorph morphol.disparity() function and have opted\r\n for this method instead.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">My apologies for bothering you all with a relatively straight forward question, but it would ease my mind knowing I didn&#39;t make some grave calculation error. My phylogenetically transformed\r\n shape data are behaving somewhat strangely in my downstream analysis and wanted to make sure this wasn&#39;t the culprit. <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">Much appreciated,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">Sarah<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">Code for clarification:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">y &lt;- shapedata<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">x &lt;- sizedata<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">C &lt;- vcv.phylo(tree)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">eigC &lt;- eigen(C)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">U &lt;- eigC$vectors<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">W &lt;- eigC$values<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">E &lt;- solve(U %*% diag(sqrt(W)) %*% t(U)) <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">y_cor &lt;- E %*% y<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">x_cor &lt;- E %*% x<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"margin-top:1.5pt;outline:none\">\r\n<div style=\"border:solid #dddddd 1.0pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 0in;outline:none\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:#f1f1f1\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><img border=\"0\" src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/x7Az90uC0FlqG1NQNJvbQl7YtYRlnWzoqu2O_ZLb9xIKhYpJarh3aZrZ_qlU6_VKMQpRwI5_nDi9FsJOqf0XSQHw_6yv1VK7rhIBScGS2g=s0-d-e1-ft#https://ssl.gstatic.com/ui/v1/icons/mail/images/cleardot.gif\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
